vendored-starlark-lsp
=====================

This crate contains code from starlark_lsp 0.14.2
(https://github.com/facebook/starlark-rust, crate `starlark_lsp`),
Copyright 2019 The Starlark in Rust Authors and Copyright (c) Facebook, Inc.
and its affiliates, licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0 (see
LICENSE in this directory).

heph owns this copy. Bugs are fixed in place; there is no verbatim refresh at
starlark releases, and an upstream fix is ported by hand when it matters to
BUILD files. Every divergence from 0.14.2 is listed below with its reason.

Copied unchanged
----------------
src/bind.rs, src/completion.rs, src/docs.rs, src/error.rs, src/exported.rs,
src/inspect.rs, src/loaded.rs, src/symbols.rs.

Divergences
-----------
src/server.rs
  - The server loop is gone: `stdio_server`, `server_with_connection`,
    `main_loop`, the `send_*`/`log_message`/`publish_diagnostics` helpers, the
    `starlark/fileContents` request and the `as_request`/`as_notification`/
    `new_response`/`new_notification` glue. heph runs its own loop (its
    BUILD-file LSP's `server.rs`) and calls the analysis directly, so there is
    no JSON round-trip and no second parse per edit.
  - `Backend` is public, owns no connection, and gains `new`, `validate`
    (upstream's did_open/did_change without the notification: it returns the
    diagnostics to publish) and `close` (upstream's did_close likewise).
    `find_definition`, `completion_options`, `hover_info` and
    `server_capabilities` are public so heph's loop can route requests to them.
  - `LspOpError` is public, its `format` is public, and its `Protocol` variant
    is gone with the loop that produced it.
  - The `tests` module (driven through upstream's `TestServer` loop harness,
    `src/test.rs`) is not vendored; heph's editor-shaped harness
    (crates/plugin-buildfile/tests/lsp.rs, the `parity_*` tests) covers the
    behaviour instead.
  - `file://` URI <-> path conversion goes through `src/uri.rs` instead of
    `tower_lsp_server::UriExt`, so the crate does not depend on
    `tower-lsp-server`.

src/definition.rs
  - The test-only `FixtureWithRanges::program` helper is removed: only the
    unvendored server tests called it.

src/lib.rs
  - `definition` is a public module; `uri` is new (see above); `test` is not
    vendored.
